{"kind":"request","text":"Claude: repair a causal-trailer equality defect found while auditing retired #2921. Queue after current #21309, batch review #21341 and CI-retention #21346, before the full-scale #20084 run; preserve all remaining work and the full Tailapp I7 commitment.\n\nThe [comparison](internal/intent/envelope.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:74) joins each reference list with NUL before comparing. No references and one empty reference therefore compare equal. The [intent validator](internal/intent/intent.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:98) rejects empty signed references, but the envelope parser accepts an empty Rests-On value. An empty trailer inserted between the marker and Intent line survives actual Git storage, while the actor's valid signed intent still contains no references.\n\nI reproduced this using temporary repositories and the real [full verifier](internal/kernel/kernel.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:1523), then wrote and restored a real verification checkpoint. Both accept the malformed record. A separate [checkpoint metadata check](internal/kernel/checkpoint.go@98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7:814) accepts the same mismatch. The [probe](empty-ref-probe_test.go), [main results](main-results.txt) and [isolated comparison-change results](comparison-results.txt) are attached. Valid no-reference controls pass. In a Go overlay, using slices.Equal makes both rejection probes pass. No repository source has been changed.\n\nThis needs a valid sequencer signature and preserves the actor signature; it is an envelope/intent consistency defect, not evidence of bypassed signatures or an invented application dependency. The decoded signed refs remain the event's causal data. The [evidence and compatibility limits](empty-ref-evidence.json) record this distinction. Scanning the four current Gitseq, Tailapp, Chess and Inventory sequence histories found no empty Rests-On line, including their genesis commits. That is a bounded local scan, not a claim about every external or unreachable log.\n\nMake the smallest correction: compare references as ordered elements, preserving duplicate handling and nil/empty-list equivalence. Retain intent field validation, signature checks, object identity, payload bounds and checkpoint fallback behavior. Add focused actual-verifier and checkpoint regression coverage for the empty-trailer case alongside valid zero-reference and existing altered-reference controls. Direct comparator cases should also cover embedded separators, differing order/count and duplicates without claiming invalid signed inputs are reachable. Restore the old comparator in an isolated omission control and show the new regression catches it.\n\nThe original #2921 called this a behavior-preserving mechanical substitution. The counterexample proves that description is too narrow: this request deliberately rejects a malformed record the old verifier accepted. State that compatibility correction plainly, check the current architecture wording and update it in the same head if its contract needs clarification. Do not silently normalize malformed records or rewrite signed history. Retain the local compatibility evidence and identify any further release constraint if an affected supported history is found.\n\nUse current source bases at intake. The live internal/intent directory artifact contains the exact current envelope.go bytes; kernel.go's exact-path artifact is also byte-identical to main. The live wider kernel artifact has ordinary inherited staleness, not a superseded-world flag; preserve honest provenance. This request recovers only the EqualRefs correctness outcome discovered under #2921. It neither completes nor revives that retired multi-part mechanical sweep.","body":{"branch":"request/causal-trailer-equality","conditions":"On request/causal-trailer-equality from then-current main, enforce ordered element equality between signed references and parsed envelope trailers, preserving nil/empty list equality, order and duplicates. Valid no-reference histories still verify and restore checkpoints; an actual correctly sequencer-signed event containing an empty trailer absent from its actor-signed intent is rejected in full verification and checkpoint validation/restoration. Existing altered-reference, signature, payload/tree, fallback and bounds controls remain intact. Add targeted direct comparator cases and actual verifier/checkpoint regression evidence; an isolated restoration of the old joined comparison must fail the new regression. Record the deliberately tightened malformed-input acceptance, compatibility scope and Architecture/Security/Simplification conclusions. Reconcile current bases; update contract documentation only where needed. Run focused intent/kernel tests, required test/race/vet/build/doc gates, obtain independent exact-head review, ratify it, seal/push main and sequence with exact-path succession, verify CI and remove the owned worktree/branch. Do not rewrite existing signed records or bundle unrelated #2921 cleanup. Coordinate a later live-reader rollout separately from source delivery. Queue after21309,21341 and21346, before20084; no interruption of full I7.","head":"98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4c4f0d4142bfa057005b09e59bc0a3462980842b stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0a371f3378a44dbcfed4d24deb224d8c76a9667e, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:191ece9ae6bdc7636c4bc5c219e6af3aefb489ba, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:25846bf6b9c44bf3ec6c04b3762d78447a042aaa, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3d09b51295014affd0d1719cbe2a66a0cc2d60e9 and 4 more","target_head":"98d63376d53fcbecf0afe3fbd98639587de1bfe7","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8","to":"a5d